# What must never reach a build context, and why.
#
# Docker copies the context to the daemon before the first instruction runs, so
# an exclusion here is the only thing standing between a secret and an image
# layer. The two lines that matter most are the database and the env files:
# `apps/web/prisma/dev.db` is a real portfolio, and `apps/web/.env` holds
# SESSION_SECRET, CRON_SECRET and the VAPID private key. Neither is in git —
# which is exactly why nothing in git would have caught them being baked into
# an image and pushed to a registry.

# Secrets and state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite*
backup-*.json
android/keystore.properties
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore

# Build output and caches — the image builds its own
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/out
android/app/build
android/build
android/.gradle
.icon-cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed to run the server
.git
.github
.gitignore
docs
samples/*.fixes*.pine
.superpowers
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
